#: ../../source/destroy_README.md:9
msgid "Destroy a stream."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/destroy_README.md:11
msgid ""
"This module is meant to ensure a stream gets destroyed, handling "
"different APIs and Node.js bugs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/destroy_README.md:14
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/destroy_README.md:20
msgid "destroy(stream [, suppress])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/destroy_README.md:22
msgid ""
"Destroy the given stream, and optionally suppress any future `error` "
"events."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/destroy_README.md:24
msgid ""
"In most cases, this is identical to a simple `stream.destroy()` call. The"
" rules are as follows for a given stream:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/destroy_README.md:27
msgid ""
"If the `stream` is an instance of `ReadStream`, then call "
"`stream.destroy()` and add a listener to the `open` event to call "
"`stream.close()` if it is fired. This is for a Node.js bug that will leak"
" a file descriptor if `.destroy()` is called before `open`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/destroy_README.md:31
msgid ""
"If the `stream` is an instance of a zlib stream, then call "
"`stream.destroy()` and close the underlying zlib handle if open, "
"otherwise call `stream.close()`. This is for consistency across Node.js "
"versions and a Node.js bug that will leak a native zlib handle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/destroy_README.md:35
msgid "If the `stream` is not an instance of `Stream`, then nothing happens."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/destroy_README.md:36
msgid "If the `stream` has a `.destroy()` method, then call it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/destroy_README.md:38
msgid "The function returns the `stream` passed in as the argument."
msgstr ""

